/-! # Blueprint decomposition of Putnam 1972 A6

Classical argument: put $p_n(x) = (x - 1/2)^n$.  Since $p_n - x^n$ is a polynomial of
degree at most $n-1$, the vanishing moment conditions give
$\int_0^1 p_n(x) f(x)\,dx = \int_0^1 x^n f(x)\,dx = 1$.  If $|f(x)| < 2^n(n+1)$ almost
everywhere, then
$$1 = \Big|\int_0^1 p_n f\Big| \le \int_0^1 |p_n| |f| < 2^n(n+1) \int_0^1 |x-1/2|^n\,dx = 1,$$
a contradiction.  Hence the set $\{x \in [0,1] : |f(x)| \ge 2^n(n+1)\}$ carries
positive measure. -/

